rewritten-to-match
Same graph shape. The reference's BinaryHeap<Reverse<Node>> is a binary min-heap in two arrays (65,536 slots; it reaches 22,670 for the run parameters, measured by simulating it) ordered by (f score, vertex) as the reference's Node ordering; every pair is pushed at most once, so any correct heap pops the same sequence and the path lengths match. The g and best-f arrays are filled with i32::MAX each run. Other stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: gs, bf, hf, hv) is not logged (state is unlogged by default, so no undo log, as a Rust local has none).
